# A Report on the Open-Circuit Television Project of the University of Tennessee.

**Authors:** Bohringer, Kenneth C.

## Abstract
The history and current operation of the University of Tennessee open-circuit television project are reviewed. Planning was begun in 1972, and the first courses were broadcast during the summer of that year. Through the winter of 1975, a total of 336 students had enrolled either for credit or audit in open-circuit courses which have concentrated on the humanities and social sciences. Some student reactions to the programing are also given. (DGC)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=ED105852

